{"type":"text","timestamp":1791649321443,"sessionID":"ses_6e3a681fff4e990d127d","part":{"id":"prt_1269f05be001ROt9Hr5bgl1Dzx","sessionID":"ses_6e3a681fff4e990d127d","messageID":"msg_1269eed8e001LkfTWJmtmzyTrB","type":"text","text":"**Defect in `parser.py:2`:** `bool(value)` checks truthiness, not valid boolean strings.\n\nConfirmed:\n- `\"false\"` incorrectly returns `True` because it is nonempty.\n- Invalid inputs such as `\"yes\"`, `\"TRUE\"`, `\"\"`, and `None` return booleans instead of raising `ValueError`.\n\n**Recommended fix:** Explicitly return `True` for `\"true\"` and `False` for `\"false\"`; raise `ValueError` for everything else, without trimming or case normalization.\n\n**Prevent recurrence:** Add automated regression tests covering both valid strings and rejection of other strings, whitespace/case variants, and non-string values. Run them in CI as an enforceable guardrail.\n\nNo files were changed.","time":{"start":1791649318334,"end":1791649321443}}}
